<section id="compare" aria-labelledby="h-cmp">
  <h2 id="h-cmp" class="sec">Compare to a baseline</h2>
  <p class="sub">Per-family deltas against any run or paper model. Deltas under 2x the pass-to-pass std are labelled noise.</p>
  <details class="tool"><summary>Open the comparison</summary>
    <div class="filters"><label>Baseline <select id="cmp-base"></select></label></div>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="cmp"></table></div>
    <p class="callout" id="cmp-note"></p>
    <p class="callout">Same rule as <code>pwa compare</code>. The CSV stores only the overall std, so it is used for every family; when it is missing, the paper's pass variance (std 0.105) is used.</p>
  </details>
</section>
